  "question": {
    "text": "Electrolysis of dilute aq. $\\mathrm{NaCl}$ solution was carried out by passing $10 \\mathrm{~mA}$ current. The time required to liberate $0.01$ mole of $\\mathrm{H}_2$ gas at the cathode is (1 Faraday $=96500 \\mathrm{C} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ )",
